# Secrets. Nothing matching these should ever reach a commit.
#
# The agent reads every credential from the environment, which makes it easy to keep a
# scratch file of exports next to the code. That convenience is exactly how tokens get
# committed, so the patterns are deliberately broad.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.envrc
.tokens
.tokens.*
tokens
tokens.*
*.token
*.tokens
secrets.yaml
*-credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Editor leftovers. A vim swap file holds the full buffer, so a swap file of a token
# file is a token file.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Screenshots and scratch images. Captured while working, not part of the repo, and
# they routinely contain tokens and project identifiers in the frame.
#
# Documentation images are the exception: they live in docs/images/ under a deliberate
# name, which forces a rename and therefore a moment's thought about what is in frame.
Screenshot*.png
Screenshot*.jpg
Screen?Shot*.png
!**/docs/images/**

# Go
/bin/
/out/
*.test
coverage.out

# Compiled binaries. Go names the output after its directory, so these have no
# extension and no glob catches them.
01-slack-sre-chatbot/stack/product-catalog/product-catalog
01-slack-sre-chatbot/agent
